1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,156
One truck recall in twenty twenty-six covered

2
00:00:03,156 --> 00:00:05,682
more than four million vehicles in a

3
00:00:05,682 --> 00:00:06,664
single filing.

4
00:00:06,844 --> 00:00:09,824
One covered every Cybertruck ever sold,

5
00:00:09,824 --> 00:00:11,046
because of glue.

6
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:13,301
And one told owners not to drive

7
00:00:13,301 --> 00:00:14,598
their trucks at all,

8
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:16,219
and to park them outside.

9
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:18,682
These are the biggest truck recalls of

10
00:00:18,682 --> 00:00:21,145
twenty twenty-five and twenty twenty-six,

11
00:00:21,145 --> 00:00:21,565
ranked.

12
00:00:21,916 --> 00:00:24,804
To understand how unusual these two years

13
00:00:24,804 --> 00:00:27,411
were, you need one number from twenty

14
00:00:27,411 --> 00:00:28,046
fourteen.

15
00:00:28,226 --> 00:00:31,965
That year, General Motors issued seventy-seven recalls,

16
00:00:31,965 --> 00:00:34,208
many of them tied to its infamous

17
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:35,772
faulty ignition switch.

18
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,463
For more than a decade,

19
00:00:37,463 --> 00:00:40,485
seventy-seven was the record that no automaker

20
00:00:40,485 --> 00:00:41,536
wanted to touch.

21
00:00:41,716 --> 00:00:43,409
According to Autoblog,

22
00:00:43,409 --> 00:00:44,948
citing federal data,

23
00:00:44,948 --> 00:00:47,409
Ford passed it in just the first

24
00:00:47,409 --> 00:00:49,948
six months of twenty twenty-five.

25
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:52,480
By the end of twenty twenty-five,

26
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:55,589
Ford had issued one hundred fifty-three recalls

27
00:00:55,589 --> 00:00:58,367
covering nearly thirteen million vehicles,

28
00:00:58,367 --> 00:00:59,690
according to Motor1.

29
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:01,913
More than double the old record.

30
00:01:02,093 --> 00:01:03,408
And Automotive News,

31
00:01:03,408 --> 00:01:04,854
as quoted by Autoblog,

32
00:01:04,854 --> 00:01:07,615
reported that by mid-year Ford's count was

33
00:01:07,615 --> 00:01:10,638
higher than the next five automakers combined.

34
00:01:10,818 --> 00:01:12,889
Then twenty twenty-six arrived,

35
00:01:12,889 --> 00:01:15,293
and the single biggest recall of all

36
00:01:15,293 --> 00:01:16,496
was still to come.

37
00:01:16,845 --> 00:01:19,051
But this is not a Ford-bashing video.

38
00:01:19,231 --> 00:01:20,758
In these two years,

39
00:01:20,758 --> 00:01:22,928
Stellantis, General Motors,

40
00:01:22,928 --> 00:01:25,982
Toyota, Tesla and Rivian all had truck

41
00:01:25,982 --> 00:01:28,554
recalls that made national news.

42
00:01:28,734 --> 00:01:30,545
Some were huge and boring.

43
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:32,653
Some were tiny and frightening.

44
00:01:32,833 --> 00:01:34,425
And a few of them changed the

45
00:01:34,425 --> 00:01:36,018
way you should buy a truck in

46
00:01:36,018 --> 00:01:37,117
twenty twenty-seven.

47
00:01:37,466 --> 00:01:38,943
So we ranked ten of them,

48
00:01:38,943 --> 00:01:40,891
from the smallest to the biggest.

49
00:01:41,071 --> 00:01:42,844
And here is the twist we will

50
00:01:42,844 --> 00:01:44,067
keep coming back to.

51
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:46,314
The size of a recall tells you

52
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:48,450
how many trucks share a defect.

53
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:50,603
It does not tell you how dangerous

54
00:01:50,603 --> 00:01:50,952
it is.

55
00:01:51,132 --> 00:01:53,403
Some of the scariest recalls on this

56
00:01:53,403 --> 00:01:55,927
list cover fewer than a thousand trucks.

57
00:01:56,107 --> 00:01:58,726
Every number comes from a published source,

58
00:01:58,726 --> 00:02:00,309
listed in the description.

59
00:02:00,489 --> 00:02:02,231
Let's start at number ten.

60
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,160
First, a thirty-second lesson on how a

61
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,654
recall actually works,

62
00:02:06,654 --> 00:02:09,166
because it changes how you read every

63
00:02:09,166 --> 00:02:10,591
number in this video.

64
00:02:10,771 --> 00:02:13,133
A safety recall is filed with the

65
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,708
federal safety agency,

66
00:02:14,708 --> 00:02:17,570
NHTSA, when a manufacturer or the agency

67
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:20,361
decides a defect creates a safety risk.

68
00:02:20,541 --> 00:02:22,747
The repair is free by law.

69
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:25,523
Each recall gets a campaign number,

70
00:02:25,523 --> 00:02:28,045
like twenty-five V two seven four,

71
00:02:28,045 --> 00:02:30,863
and that number follows every truck it

72
00:02:30,863 --> 00:02:33,534
covers, no matter how many times the

73
00:02:33,534 --> 00:02:34,572
truck is sold.

74
00:02:34,921 --> 00:02:36,646
And one more thing most people do

75
00:02:36,646 --> 00:02:37,116
not know.

76
00:02:37,296 --> 00:02:39,834
A recall number counts every vehicle that

77
00:02:39,834 --> 00:02:41,197
could have the defect,

78
00:02:41,197 --> 00:02:42,497
not the ones that do.

79
00:02:42,677 --> 00:02:45,527
Rivian estimated about one percent of its

80
00:02:45,527 --> 00:02:48,099
recalled trucks were really affected.

81
00:02:48,279 --> 00:02:50,224
Ram said the same about one of

82
00:02:50,224 --> 00:02:52,168
its stability control recalls.

83
00:02:52,348 --> 00:02:54,925
So a recall of a million trucks

84
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:57,584
may involve far fewer bad parts.

85
00:02:57,764 --> 00:03:00,561
The manufacturer recalls the whole range because

86
00:03:00,561 --> 00:03:02,658
it cannot tell which trucks have the

87
00:03:02,658 --> 00:03:04,115
problem without checking.

88
00:03:04,464 --> 00:03:07,294
Number ten is the Rivian R one

89
00:03:07,294 --> 00:03:07,483
T.

90
00:03:07,663 --> 00:03:09,977
In January twenty twenty-six,

91
00:03:09,977 --> 00:03:12,690
Rivian recalled nineteen thousand,

92
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:15,164
six hundred forty-one vehicles,

93
00:03:15,164 --> 00:03:18,196
twelve thousand, six hundred ten R one

94
00:03:18,196 --> 00:03:21,628
T pickups and seven thousand and thirty-one

95
00:03:21,628 --> 00:03:22,665
R one S SUVs,

96
00:03:22,665 --> 00:03:26,495
from the twenty twenty-two to twenty twenty-five

97
00:03:26,495 --> 00:03:29,687
model years, according to The EV Report.

98
00:03:29,867 --> 00:03:32,225
The problem was a rear suspension toe

99
00:03:32,225 --> 00:03:35,092
link joint that could separate while driving.

100
00:03:35,441 --> 00:03:36,602
Here is the twist.

101
00:03:36,782 --> 00:03:38,941
This defect did not come from the

102
00:03:38,941 --> 00:03:39,464
factory.

103
00:03:39,644 --> 00:03:41,583
It came from the service department.

104
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:44,304
The joint may not have been reassembled

105
00:03:44,304 --> 00:03:47,432
correctly during service work done between April

106
00:03:47,432 --> 00:03:50,494
twenty twenty-two and March twenty twenty-five.

107
00:03:50,674 --> 00:03:51,630
In other words,

108
00:03:51,630 --> 00:03:54,180
a repair could have created the problem.

109
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,147
Rivian estimated only about one percent of

110
00:03:57,147 --> 00:04:00,200
the recalled vehicles actually had the defect.

111
00:04:00,549 --> 00:04:02,488
But Rivian's advice was blunt.

112
00:04:02,668 --> 00:04:04,675
Owners were told not to drive the

113
00:04:04,675 --> 00:04:07,351
affected vehicles, and to park them outside,

114
00:04:07,351 --> 00:04:08,810
according to the report.

115
00:04:08,990 --> 00:04:11,586
A joint separating at speed could raise

116
00:04:11,586 --> 00:04:13,982
the risk of a crash without warning.

117
00:04:14,162 --> 00:04:16,140
The fix was new bolts with an

118
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:18,458
updated procedure, free of charge.

119
00:04:18,638 --> 00:04:20,852
And the lesson for any truck owner

120
00:04:20,852 --> 00:04:21,958
is a strange one.

121
00:04:22,138 --> 00:04:23,056
After a repair,

122
00:04:23,056 --> 00:04:25,013
the work itself can be the thing

123
00:04:25,013 --> 00:04:26,237
that needs checking.

124
00:04:26,586 --> 00:04:29,086
Number nine is the smallest recall on

125
00:04:29,086 --> 00:04:31,924
our list, and maybe the most uncomfortable

126
00:04:31,924 --> 00:04:32,194
one.

127
00:04:32,374 --> 00:04:34,331
In March twenty twenty-five,

128
00:04:34,331 --> 00:04:37,897
Ford recalled nine hundred fifty twenty twenty-four

129
00:04:37,897 --> 00:04:40,203
F-150 Lightning electric pickups,

130
00:04:40,203 --> 00:04:42,301
according to Kelley Blue Book.

131
00:04:42,481 --> 00:04:45,709
Ford said a supplier's production deviations may

132
00:04:45,709 --> 00:04:49,341
have misaligned the electrodes inside the high-voltage

133
00:04:49,341 --> 00:04:50,283
battery cells.

134
00:04:50,632 --> 00:04:51,689
Why does that matter?

135
00:04:51,869 --> 00:04:54,683
Over repeated charging and discharging,

136
00:04:54,683 --> 00:04:57,858
a misaligned electrode can cause an internal

137
00:04:57,858 --> 00:05:00,239
short circuit, and that is a fire

138
00:05:00,239 --> 00:05:00,600
risk.

139
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,489
Until the repair was done,

140
00:05:02,489 --> 00:05:04,922
owners were asked to keep the battery

141
00:05:04,922 --> 00:05:06,828
charged below eighty percent.

142
00:05:07,008 --> 00:05:08,783
Think about that for an electric truck

143
00:05:08,783 --> 00:05:09,063
owner.

144
00:05:09,243 --> 00:05:10,823
You paid for a big battery,

145
00:05:10,823 --> 00:05:12,696
and the safety advice was to use

146
00:05:12,696 --> 00:05:13,632
only part of it.

147
00:05:13,981 --> 00:05:15,375
Here is the twist.

148
00:05:15,555 --> 00:05:18,174
Nine hundred fifty trucks is almost nothing

149
00:05:18,174 --> 00:05:20,123
next to the millions we will see

150
00:05:20,123 --> 00:05:20,489
later.

151
00:05:20,669 --> 00:05:22,288
But this is the kind of recall

152
00:05:22,288 --> 00:05:24,338
that matters most to the people inside

153
00:05:24,338 --> 00:05:24,500
it.

154
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:27,168
A small recall can be serious,

155
00:05:27,168 --> 00:05:29,241
and a big recall can be a

156
00:05:29,241 --> 00:05:30,485
software patch.

157
00:05:30,665 --> 00:05:31,845
Keep that in mind,

158
00:05:31,845 --> 00:05:34,138
because number eight is also small,

159
00:05:34,138 --> 00:05:36,301
and it involves a part that holds

160
00:05:36,301 --> 00:05:38,397
your front wheels to the engine.

161
00:05:38,747 --> 00:05:41,278
Number eight is the Toyota Tacoma.

162
00:05:41,458 --> 00:05:43,610
In October twenty twenty-five,

163
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:47,267
Toyota recalled about six thousand brand-new twenty

164
00:05:47,267 --> 00:05:50,351
twenty-five Tacoma four-wheel-drive trucks,

165
00:05:50,351 --> 00:05:52,000
according to TFL Truck.

166
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:54,568
The front driveshaft joints may have been

167
00:05:54,568 --> 00:05:56,665
made without the required materials,

168
00:05:56,665 --> 00:05:58,762
and they could deform or break while

169
00:05:58,762 --> 00:05:59,228
driving.

170
00:05:59,408 --> 00:06:02,261
Dealers check the driveshaft serial number and

171
00:06:02,261 --> 00:06:03,564
replace it if needed.

172
00:06:03,913 --> 00:06:06,047
Six thousand trucks is not a big

173
00:06:06,047 --> 00:06:06,514
number.

174
00:06:06,694 --> 00:06:08,412
But it lands on a truck that

175
00:06:08,412 --> 00:06:10,131
has a reputation to protect.

176
00:06:10,311 --> 00:06:12,306
The Tacoma is one of the most

177
00:06:12,306 --> 00:06:14,714
popular midsize pickups in America,

178
00:06:14,714 --> 00:06:17,466
and people buy it precisely because they

179
00:06:17,466 --> 00:06:18,705
expect it to last.

180
00:06:18,885 --> 00:06:20,382
And it was not the first time.

181
00:06:20,562 --> 00:06:22,632
In February twenty twenty-four,

182
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:26,303
Toyota recalled about three hundred eighty-one thousand

183
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:29,641
twenty twenty-two and twenty twenty-three Tacomas,

184
00:06:29,641 --> 00:06:32,245
because welding debris on the rear axle

185
00:06:32,245 --> 00:06:34,715
could make the retaining nuts loosen.

186
00:06:35,064 --> 00:06:36,722
If those nuts came off,

187
00:06:36,722 --> 00:06:39,245
a part could separate from the axle

188
00:06:39,245 --> 00:06:41,624
and affect stability and braking.

189
00:06:41,804 --> 00:06:44,028
The fix was an inspection and a

190
00:06:44,028 --> 00:06:46,181
re-tightening, free of charge.

191
00:06:46,361 --> 00:06:48,207
So here is the twist.

192
00:06:48,387 --> 00:06:51,880
The brand with the strongest reliability reputation

193
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:54,482
in trucks had two driveline recalls in

194
00:06:54,482 --> 00:06:55,167
two years.

195
00:06:55,347 --> 00:06:58,528
A reputation is built over decades.

196
00:06:58,708 --> 00:07:00,758
A recall can come from a single

197
00:07:00,758 --> 00:07:02,807
bad batch at a single supplier.

198
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:05,920
Number seven is the Tesla Cybertruck.

199
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,481
On March twentieth,

200
00:07:07,481 --> 00:07:11,625
twenty twenty-five, Tesla recalled forty-six thousand and

201
00:07:11,625 --> 00:07:15,477
ninety-six Cybertrucks, every one built from November

202
00:07:15,477 --> 00:07:17,804
thirteenth, twenty twenty-three,

203
00:07:17,804 --> 00:07:19,548
the start of deliveries,

204
00:07:19,548 --> 00:07:21,875
through February twenty-seventh,

205
00:07:21,875 --> 00:07:25,001
twenty twenty-five, according to CarScoops.

206
00:07:25,181 --> 00:07:28,176
In practice, that was basically every Cybertruck

207
00:07:28,176 --> 00:07:29,674
on the road at the time.

208
00:07:30,023 --> 00:07:32,547
The problem was a stainless steel panel

209
00:07:32,547 --> 00:07:33,905
called the cant rail,

210
00:07:33,905 --> 00:07:36,170
which runs along the roof above the

211
00:07:36,170 --> 00:07:36,688
windows.

212
00:07:36,868 --> 00:07:39,399
It could partially come off while driving.

213
00:07:39,579 --> 00:07:42,098
And the reason is almost unbelievable for

214
00:07:42,098 --> 00:07:44,188
a truck sold as being bulletproof.

215
00:07:44,368 --> 00:07:46,659
The panel was held on entirely by

216
00:07:46,659 --> 00:07:48,048
structural adhesive.

217
00:07:48,228 --> 00:07:48,518
Glue.

218
00:07:48,698 --> 00:07:51,308
And that adhesive could become brittle from

219
00:07:51,308 --> 00:07:52,704
environmental exposure.

220
00:07:53,053 --> 00:07:54,284
Here is the twist.

221
00:07:54,464 --> 00:07:57,586
Most of Tesla's earlier recalls were fixed

222
00:07:57,586 --> 00:07:59,221
with software updates,

223
00:07:59,221 --> 00:08:00,559
sent over the air.

224
00:08:00,739 --> 00:08:02,063
This one could not be.

225
00:08:02,243 --> 00:08:04,495
Owners had to bring the truck in,

226
00:08:04,495 --> 00:08:06,678
and Tesla added a stud welded to

227
00:08:06,678 --> 00:08:09,135
the panel and clamped to the truck's

228
00:08:09,135 --> 00:08:10,568
structure with a nut,

229
00:08:10,568 --> 00:08:12,274
plus a stronger adhesive.

230
00:08:12,454 --> 00:08:14,020
According to CarScoops,

231
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:16,811
it was the eighth Cybertruck recall since

232
00:08:16,811 --> 00:08:17,969
deliveries began.

233
00:08:18,149 --> 00:08:19,832
In about sixteen months.

234
00:08:20,182 --> 00:08:22,440
And the Cybertruck story did not stop

235
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:22,806
there.

236
00:08:22,986 --> 00:08:24,777
In May twenty twenty-six,

237
00:08:24,777 --> 00:08:29,004
Tesla recalled Cybertrucks with eighteen-inch steel wheels,

238
00:08:29,004 --> 00:08:32,227
because rough roads and cornering could crack

239
00:08:32,227 --> 00:08:34,663
the brake rotor stud holes and let

240
00:08:34,663 --> 00:08:36,168
wheel studs separate,

241
00:08:36,168 --> 00:08:39,391
according to federal data reported by iHeart.

242
00:08:39,571 --> 00:08:42,266
Tesla said there were no reported crashes

243
00:08:42,266 --> 00:08:43,054
or injuries.

244
00:08:43,234 --> 00:08:45,381
The fix was new rotors,

245
00:08:45,381 --> 00:08:47,061
hubs and lug nuts,

246
00:08:47,061 --> 00:08:48,087
at no cost.

247
00:08:48,437 --> 00:08:50,771
Number six is the Toyota Tundra.

248
00:08:50,951 --> 00:08:53,065
In January twenty twenty-six,

249
00:08:53,065 --> 00:08:56,929
Toyota recalled one hundred sixty-two thousand twenty

250
00:08:56,929 --> 00:09:00,720
twenty-four and twenty twenty-five Tundra and Tundra

251
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,490
Hybrid pickups, according to Autoblog.

252
00:09:03,670 --> 00:09:06,618
The rearview camera display could get stuck

253
00:09:06,618 --> 00:09:07,921
on the camera view,

254
00:09:07,921 --> 00:09:09,498
or show a black screen.

255
00:09:09,678 --> 00:09:11,248
Since twenty eighteen,

256
00:09:11,248 --> 00:09:14,460
federal rules have required backup cameras on

257
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:17,030
new vehicles, so a camera that fails

258
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,386
is a safety recall,

259
00:09:18,386 --> 00:09:19,814
not a comfort issue.

260
00:09:20,163 --> 00:09:22,416
The fix was a free software update

261
00:09:22,416 --> 00:09:24,471
to the parking assist computer.

262
00:09:24,651 --> 00:09:27,500
But the Tundra's bigger recall story started

263
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,018
earlier.

264
00:09:28,198 --> 00:09:29,750
In twenty twenty-four,

265
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:33,207
Toyota recalled about one hundred thousand twenty

266
00:09:33,207 --> 00:09:36,876
twenty-two and twenty twenty-three Tundras and about

267
00:09:36,876 --> 00:09:39,699
three thousand five hundred Lexus LX six

268
00:09:39,699 --> 00:09:43,085
hundreds, because machining debris may have been

269
00:09:43,085 --> 00:09:44,708
left inside the engine,

270
00:09:44,708 --> 00:09:46,613
which could cause knocking,

271
00:09:46,613 --> 00:09:48,589
rough running, and stalling,

272
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,988
according to the Associated Press.

273
00:09:51,337 --> 00:09:52,765
And here is the twist.

274
00:09:52,945 --> 00:09:55,501
Toyota's remedy for that one was to

275
00:09:55,501 --> 00:09:58,642
replace the entire engine on every affected

276
00:09:58,642 --> 00:10:00,248
truck, free of charge.

277
00:10:00,428 --> 00:10:01,171
Not a part.

278
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:02,454
Not an inspection.

279
00:10:02,634 --> 00:10:03,702
A whole engine.

280
00:10:03,882 --> 00:10:06,506
Toyota did not say what it cost.

281
00:10:06,686 --> 00:10:09,147
